{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21fe7e39d99b57bc5bdf", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Statistics - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 75, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffe3"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff9a", "title": "Mathematics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff2f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d802"], "concepts": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d7c7"], "question": {"text": "<p>If for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>, the frequency distribution of the marks obtained by <math><mn>20</mn></math> students in a test is:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Marks</td>\t\t\t<td>2</td>\t\t\t<td>3</td>\t\t\t<td>5</td>\t\t\t<td>7</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Frequency distribution</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Then the mean of the marks is :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b9020d", "text": "<math><mn>3.0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff30"}, {"id": "4f38c1", "text": "<math><mn>2.5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff31"}, {"id": "46c84b", "text": "<math><mn>3.2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff32"}, {"id": "b0008c", "text": "<math><mn>2.8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff33"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff34", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d825"], "concepts": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d7ed"], "question": {"text": "Marks obtains by all the students of class 12 are presented in a freqency distribution with classes of equal width. Let the median of this grouped data be 14 with median class interval 12-18 and median class frequency 12 . If the number of students whose marks are less than 12 is 18 , then the total number of students is"}, "options": [{"id": "ec7a9e", "text": "$52$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff35"}, {"id": "b20dd2", "text": "$48$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff36"}, {"id": "68379a", "text": "$44$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff37"}, {"id": "8f0a36", "text": "$40$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff38"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff39", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d918"], "concepts": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d8ef"], "question": {"text": "If the mean deviation about median for the number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;arranged in the ascending order, is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> then the median is"}, "options": [{"id": "8a285e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff3a"}, {"id": "b7502b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff3b"}, {"id": "8a275e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff3c"}, {"id": "e61ef4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff3d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff3e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbf6ed13040ec85d9fd"], "concepts": ["6162fcbf6ed13040ec85d9da"], "question": {"text": "The frequency distribution of the age of students in a class of 40 students is given below.\n$\\begin{array}{|l|c|c|c|c|l|l|}\n\\hline \\text{Age} & 15 & 16 & 17 & 18 & 19 & 20 \\\\\n\\hline \\text{No of Students} & 5 & 8 & 5 & 12 & x & y \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$\nIf the mean deviation about the median is 1.25, then $4 x+5 y$ is equal to :"}, "options": [{"id": "59d239", "text": "46", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff3f"}, {"id": "83b554", "text": "43", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff40"}, {"id": "3af4fb", "text": "44", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff41"}, {"id": "b8b58a", "text": "47", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff42"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff43", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d918"], "concepts": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d8eb"], "question": {"text": "If the mean and the standard deviation of the data&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> respectively, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> are the roots of the equation:"}, "options": [{"id": "8b0c86", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff44"}, {"id": "d18fea", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff45"}, {"id": "a0604e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff46"}, {"id": "6581b2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff47"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff48", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d802"], "concepts": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d7c7"], "question": {"text": "If the sum of the deviations of <math><mn>50</mn></math> observations from <math><mn>30</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>, then the mean of these observations is :"}, "options": [{"id": "9a9333", "text": "<math><mn>30</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff49"}, {"id": "669014", "text": "<math><mn>51</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff4a"}, {"id": "f9c3b1", "text": "<math><mn>50</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff4b"}, {"id": "a67009", "text": "<math><mn>31</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff4c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff4d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d825"], "concepts": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d7ed"], "question": {"text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> denote the median of the following frequency distribution.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\" columnlines=\"solid\" frame=\"solid\" rowlines=\"solid\"><mtr><mtd><mtext> Class </mtext></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext> Frequency </mtext></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>9</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>10</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>8</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is equal to :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ee5093", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>416</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff4e"}, {"id": "f2f327", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>104</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff4f"}, {"id": "77299a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>52</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff50"}, {"id": "0b6c4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>208</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff51"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff52", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbf6ed13040ec85d9fd"], "concepts": ["6162fcbf6ed13040ec85d9da"], "question": {"text": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbf{R}$. Let the mean and the variance of 6 observations $-3,4,7,-6, \\alpha, \\beta$ be 2 and 23 , respectively. The mean deviation about the mean of these 6 observations is :"}, "options": [{"id": "79326f", "text": "$\\frac{13}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff53"}, {"id": "d1a802", "text": "$\\frac{16}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff54"}, {"id": "df93e0", "text": "$\\frac{11}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff55"}, {"id": "9fc2f3", "text": "$\\frac{14}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff56"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff57", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d918"], "concepts": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d8f9"], "question": {"text": "The mean and variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;observations are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math> respetively. If two observations are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the variance of the remaining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> observations is :"}, "options": [{"id": "95dc7d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>92</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff58"}, {"id": "94b401", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>134</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff59"}, {"id": "97b74d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>112</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff5a"}, {"id": "a07e71", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>536</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff5b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ff5c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d825"], "concepts": ["6162fcbd6ed13040ec85d7ed"], "question": {"text": "The mean and the median of the following ten numbers in increasing order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>22</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>29</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>34</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>42</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>67</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>70</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi></math> are <math><mn>42</mn></math> and <math><mn>35</mn></math> respectively, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to:"}, "options": [{"id": "48c09a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "