o>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "0f4e0f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffc9"}, {"id": "50db0f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffca"}, {"id": "6e68ab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffcb"}, {"id": "4af17f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffcc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffcd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d918"], "concepts": ["6162fcbe6ed13040ec85d8f9"], "question": {"text": "The variance of the numbers $8,21,34,47, \\ldots, 320$ is"}, "options": [{"id": "9ca2c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffce"}, {"id": "3a7655", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffcf"}, {"id": "688834", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffd0"}, {"id": "63fed5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffd1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffd2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2faad66f9ce3f243b4573"], "topics": ["6162fcbf6ed13040ec85d9fd"], "concepts": ["6162fcbf6ed13040ec85d9da"], "question": {"text": "From a lot of 10 items, which include 3 defective items, a sample of 5 items is drawn at random. Let the random variable $\\mathrm{X}$ denote the number of defective items in the sample. If the variance of $\\mathrm{X}$ is $\\sigma^2$, then $96 \\sigma^2$ is equal to ______"}, "options": [{"id": "491fa4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffd3"}, {"id": "1d540b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffd4"}, {"id": "8849e6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6b2ee0e063d927ffd5"}, {"id": "358186", "text": "", "isCorrect": nu